Deployment
==========
Deployment will create replicaset and maintain multiple revisions of deployments.
INternally deployment controller will use replicaset to create and manage PODs.

Deployment ==>> ReplicaSet ==>> Create and Manage PODs.

Deployment controller supports deployment strategies like deploying applicaitons without any downtime.

Deployment controller ensures that only certain number of PODs are down while they are being updated to a new version.
By default,
It ensures that atleast 75% of desired number of PODs are up and 25% of maximum unavailable.

Recreate.
RollingUpdate. [Default]

With Recreate deployment strategy,
All old PODs are killed at once and get replaced at once with new PODs.

We can have some downtime with recreate deployment strategy.

RollingUpdate deploymnet is standard default deployment strategy to kubenretes.
It works slowly - one by one,
replacing POds of previous version of applications with PODs of new version without any cluster downtime.

When there is a probelem,
Deployment can be aborted without bringing the cluster down.

nano Deployment_Recreate.yaml            #Recreate
 
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: maven-deployment
  namespace: production
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      application: maven
  strategy:
    type: Recreate
  template:
    metadata:
      name: maven-pod
      labels:
        application: maven
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: maven-container
        image: mithuntechnologies/maven-web-application:1
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8080
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: maven-service
  namespace: production
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    application: maven
  ports:
  - port: 80
    targetPort: 8080

