HPA - Horizontal POD Autoscaling
================================

We always deploy PODs with minimum 2 POD replicas.

K8s POD Autoscaling will make sure that we have minimum number of POD replicas available at any time.
K8s POD autoscaling can scale up and scale down PODs based on the observed CPU and memory utilization.

Types of POD Autoscaling,
VPA
HPA

Vertical POD Autoscaling,
VPC is a process of increasing CPU and memory for same running POD,
Whenever there is more load,
Resource capacity for an existing POD will be increase to server end user traffic.

HPA
Horizontal POD Autoscaling
HPA is a process of creating multiple PODs with required CPU and memory.
Whenever there is a load,
Multiple PODs will be created based on load using existing POD specifications [CPU and Memory].

We use HPA for 97% of times.

We must set resources requets and resources limits for the PODs.
When we don't set esources requets and resources limits,
HPA won't be able to scale up and scale down PODs based on CPU utilization.

