PersistentVolume and PersistentVolumeClaim
==========================================
PersistentVolume and PersistentVolumeClaim are kubernetes objects.
PersistentVolume and PersistentVolumeClaim should be used to attach volume/storage to a POD.

Persistent Volume
=================
PV is nothing but a storage [hostpath and nfs storage etc] in k8s cluster.
PersistentVolume will exist independently from a POD life cycle which is consuming the storage.

PVs are not created in any namespace as they're cluster scoped resources.

PersistentVolumeClaim
=====================
PersistentVolumeClaim is a request for storage [PV] to a pOD.
When POD requires access to storage, POD will get an access to PV with the help of PVC.
PVC will be used in POD as a volume, PVC will be attached to PV.

PVC claim created in custom namespace, can get access to PV persistentvolume created in default namespace as PV is cluster level storage.

PV can be provisioned in 2 ways,
Manually.
Dynamically.

Static Volumes - Manual Provisioning,
K8s administorator will create persistent volumes manually so that PVs can be available for PODs which requires.

Dynamic Volumes - Automatically provisioning,
Dynamic volumes are provisioined automatically by a storage class.
When we create a PVC, if PV is not available then storage class will create persistentvolume dynamically.

PersistentVolume Access Modes
============================
ReadWriteOnce - RWO
ReadOnlyMany - ROX
ReadWriteMany - RWX
ReadWriteOncePOD - RWOP

PV can only be mounted using once access mode at a time, even it supports many access modes.

Reclaim Policies
================
Retain - When PVC is deleted then persistentvoulme remains.
Delete - When PVC is deleted then Persistentvolume is deleted.

ReclaimPolicy should be set to retain for production environments.
ReclaimPolicy should be set to delete in Non Production Environments.

Default Reclaim Policy for a storage class will be set to delete.

