kubectl describe node ip-10-0-0-14

cat /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml     #to check




Taints are added on the nodes.
Tolerations are added on the PODs.

Effects in Taint
================
We have 3 effects while tainting nodes.

NoSchedule,
NoSchedule works only with New PODs.

NoExecute,
NoExecute works with New PODs as well as with existing PODs.
Existing PODs, when taints are added to worker nodes, any existing pod not tolerating the Taint with effect noexecute will be removed from worker node and rescheduled in other available worker node.

PreferNoSchedule,
It sometimes works and sometimes won't work.

Operators in Tolerations
========================
We've 3 operators in Tolerations.

Equal,
Taint value on a node must match the tolerations value on the POD for the POD to tolerate the Taint.

Taint,
environment=production:NoSchedule

tolerations:
- key: "Equal"
  value: "production"
  effect: "NoSchedule"
  
NotEqual
Taint value on a node should not match the Tolerations value on the POD.
When Taint value is different, the POD will tolerate the Taint.

Taint: environemt=production:NoExecute

tolerations:
- key: "environment"
  operator: "NoEqual"
  value: "development"
  effect: "NoExecute"
  
Exists
POD will tolerate the taint but the value of the taint doesn't matter that's the Key is important but the value is not.

Taint: environemt:NoSchedule

tolerations:
- key: "environemt"
  operator: "Exists"
  effect: "NoSchedule"

Taint Node,
<Key>=<Value>:<Effect>
environment=development:NoSchedule
environment=production:NoExecute


