POD Disruption Budget
=====================
PDB is a k8s object that specifies minimum number of PODs that must remain avaiable during discruption cuased by voluntary actions and involuntarts actions.

Voluntary actions,
Draining Worker Node.
Scaling Down Worker Node.
We might delete a POD mistakenly.
We might mistakenly delete the deployment or other controllers which are responsible for managing PODs.

Involuntary Actions.
Node Failures.
Cluster administrator might delete worker node mistakenly.

We must ensure PDB that we create allows some disruptions.
POD Replicas 5 ==>> PDB Replicas 5.
We need to ensure the Result of PDB is allowedDisruption>=1 =>> 0.
We should use % based PDB.
We should never create a PDB for a deploying running with only a single POD as it will never be a valid.


