Git Branch and Git Tag
======================
Git branch is used for ongoing wokr which moves forward and git tag is a saved version which is stayed fixed.

Git branch is like a separate working copy of the repository before adding it to the final version.
Git branch is used when we want to add a new feature or fix a bug etc.
As and when we keep committing changes, the branch automatially updated to inclue the latest changes.
Many people can work on different branches at a same time without disturbing each other.
When work is completed, the branch can be merged back into the main project.

Git Tag.
Git tag is like specific version of repository to which we can always come back to respective release.
Git tag is usually used to mark important version like a final release.
Once we create a tag, it doesn't change.
Git tag helps to find stable and released version later.
Git tags are often named with version numbers like v1.1.1 and v2.1.1 etc.


