Prerequisites to Upgrade Kubernetes Cluster
===========================================
We Need to Go Through Release Notes [Change Logs] Which Explains about Changes Happening from Old Version to New Version.
We Need to Cordon Worker Nodes to Make Sure That Worker Nodes are Unschedulable During an Upgrade.
We Should Always Perform Cluster Upgrades in Lower Environments like Development and Staging Before Upgrading Production Cluster.
We Need to Make Sure that Control Plane and Worker Nodes are Having Same Version.
We Need to Make Sure that Cluster Autoscaler Matches With Control Plane Version.
We Need to Make Sure that Kubelet Version is also in Sync to Match Control Plane Version.
We Need to Make Sure that Backups are Taken for Workloads, Persistentvolumes and Secrets Etc Before Performing Cluster Upgrade.

Commands to Upgrade EKS Cluster using AWS CLI
=============================================
Get Current Kubernetes Version of EKS Cluster
aws eks describe-cluster --name Production --region ap-south-1 --query 'cluster.version' --output text

Upgrade EKS Kubernetes Control Plane
aws eks update-cluster-version --name Production --region ap-south-1 --kubernetes-version 1.33

aws eks describe-cluster --name Production --region ap-south-1 --query "cluster.status" --output text
Control Plane Upgrade Will be Completed When Cluster Status Changes to Active.

aws eks describe-cluster --name Production --region ap-south-1 --query 'cluster.version' --output text
Elastic Kubernetes Control Plane Version Should be Updated as Expected.

Get Current Version of Cluster Node Group
aws eks describe-nodegroup --cluster-name Production --region ap-south-1 --nodegroup-name Production_Node_Group --query "nodegroup.version" --output text

aws eks update-nodegroup-version --cluster-name Production --region ap-south-1 --nodegroup-name Production_Node_Group --kubernetes-version 1.33
Upgrading NodeGroup Takes Time Based on the Number of Worker Nodes Part of Cluster.

aws eks describe-nodegroup --cluster-name Production --region ap-south-1 --nodegroup-name Production_Node_Group --query "nodegroup.status" --output text
Cluster Node Group Upgrade Will be Completed When Node Group Status Changes to Active.

aws eks describe-nodegroup --cluster-name Production --region ap-south-1 --nodegroup-name Production_Node_Group --query "nodegroup.version" --output text
Cluster Node Group Version Should be Updated as Expected.

Alternatively,
We Can Create New Node Group With Latest Version With Set of Worker Nodes,
Then Scale Down Old Worker Nodes and Delete Old Node Group Which is Often a Simple Approach.

Update KubeConfig File to Ensure That It Points to Newly Upgraded Cluster
aws eks update-kubeconfig --region ap-south-1 --name Production

Upgrade Add-Ons
Amazon EKS Provides Several Managed Add-Ons like AWS_VPC_CNI and Core_DNS Etc.
We Need to Upgrade Add-Ons to be Compatible With New Kubernetes Version After Upgrading Kubernetes Version.

aws eks update-addon --cluster-name Production --region ap-south-1 --addon-name vpc-cni --addon-version v1.19.2-eksbuild.1
aws eks update-addon --cluster-name Production --region ap-south-1 --addon-name coredns --addon-version v1.11.1-eksbuild.9

We Need to Make Sure All PODs are Running and There are No Issues With the Worker Nodes.
Kubernetes Control Plane, Node Group, Add-Ons Should be Upgraded and PODs Should be Up and Running as Expected.


